Here are some quick notes that can let you set up a machine for use with SMOG 2

These notes were uses to set up an Ubuntu VM for use in a workshop

Once ubuntu was installed via an image, then log in and:

# prep for smog2

sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get upgrade -y
sudo apt-get install -y --noinstall-recommends cpanminus vim git-all patch pdl default-jre libxml-simple-perl nano emacs make
cpanm String::Util Exporter XML::Validator::Schema



#smog2

mkdir ~/BIN/smog2.4.5-pre1
cd ~/BIN/smog2.4.5-pre1
git clone -n https://github.com/smog-server/SMOG2.git .
git checkout tags/v2.4.5-pre1
rm -rf .git
source configure.smog2


# install OpenSMOG
wget https://repo.anaconda.com/miniconda/Miniconda3-latest-Linux-x86_64.sh

chmod u+x Miniconda3-latest-Linux-x86_64.sh

./Miniconda3-latest-Linux-x86_64.sh
just install into base
conda install -c conda-forge OpenSMOG

# we want to use a newer version than available on conda

git clone https://github.com/smog-server/OpenSMOG.git
cp both .py files  and share to the conda directory


# use web browser to download and VMD
